<title>SINGAPORE: L.C. Development JV buys Singapore complex.</title>
<headline>L.C. Development JV buys Singapore complex.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>L.C. Development Ltd said on Thursday it had agreed with state gaming firm Singapore Pools (Pte) Ltd to set up a 50:50 joint venture to buy a Singapore shopping and office complex for Singapore $145 million.</p>
<p>L.C. Development, the property arm of Lum Chang Holdings Ltd, said in a statement the deal to buy the nine-storey Paradiz Centre was signed on October 16.</p>
<p>The deal would not materially affect L.C. Development's net tangible asset backing per share or its earnings per share for the financial year to June 30, 1997, it said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
